.TH GRPC-CA-PROVIDER 1 "2026-07-18" "Agentic Sandbox" "Enterprise CA Provider Protocol"
.SH NAME
grpc-ca-provider \- implement the Agentic Sandbox certificate-provider command protocol
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grpc-ca-provider
.I describe
.br
.B grpc-ca-provider
.I trust-bundle
.br
.B grpc-ca-provider
.I sign
.br
.B grpc-ca-provider
.I health
.br
.B grpc-ca-provider
.I serve
.RI " [ options ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
An Agentic Sandbox CA provider is an explicitly configured executable.
Management starts it directly, without a shell or PATH lookup, sends one
bounded JSON request on standard input, reads one bounded JSON response on
standard output, and waits for exit.
.PP
The baseline commands are on-demand and do not require a resident service.
High-throughput providers may implement
.B serve
using the same logical protocol over an owner-only local socket.
.PP
Standard error is reserved for non-secret diagnostics. Providers must never
write private keys, provider tokens, passphrases, HSM PINs, or resolved
credential values to standard output, standard error, logs, traces, metrics,
or crash reports.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B describe
Return protocol major/minor version, implementation identity, build
provenance, and capabilities. Takes no request body.
.TP
.B trust-bundle
Read a TrustBundleRequest and return the complete bundle, trust domain,
request ID, and immutable revision.
.TP
.B sign
Read a SignWorkloadCsrRequest and return a certificate chain for the authorized
SPIFFE ID. The provider receives a CSR and never a leaf private key.
.TP
.B health
Return ready, degraded, or unavailable state with a bounded non-secret
diagnostics code.
.TP
.B serve
Optional persistent mode for fleet-scale throughput. It must preserve protocol
v1 semantics and use a management-owned local socket. TCP is not enabled by
default.
.SH SECRET REFERENCES
Provider configuration may identify a workload identity, HSM or PKCS#11
handle, inherited file descriptor, operating-system credential-store item, or
owner-only configuration file. These are opaque references. Raw secret values
must not be accepted as command-line arguments or protocol fields.
.PP
Examples and agent-readable help must use synthetic reference names such as
.B openbao-role://fleet-agent
and must not encourage printing, copying, or exporting secret contents.
.SH DISCOVERY
Adapters must implement
.BR --help .
Packages should provide shell completions and machine-readable schema/help
alongside this manual. Management accepts only an explicitly configured
absolute executable path; ambient executable discovery is prohibited.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates a valid protocol response was written. Nonzero indicates the
operation failed; management suppresses provider diagnostics from client-facing
responses and fails issuance closed.
.SH SECURITY
Management independently validates protocol version, required capabilities,
request correlation, SPIFFE URI-SAN, CSR public-key match, certificate
signature, trust domain, bundle revision, and TTL.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I docs/security/enterprise-ca-provider-contract.md
Public responsibility split and protocol overview.
.TP
.I .aiwg/architecture/adr/ADR-031-enterprise-certificate-provider-boundary.md
Controlling architecture decision.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agentic-mgmt (1),
.BR grpc-local-ca (1)
